wiki-cn.wikidot.com/the-donkman-s-den">驴哥的窝点 中心页</a> - Donkman's Den Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/midnight-neon">子夜霓都</a> - Midnight in the Neon City</li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Russian -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-3911">SCP-3911 - Шип бога</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/lovataar-throne">О Ловатаар и Троне</a> - Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/anthropological-report-darkwater">Антропологический подход к саркицизму — Социологический портрет 03: Ложа Тёмных Вод</a> - Darkwater Report</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/the-machine">Сизифова Машина</a> - The Sisyphean Machine</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-5862">SCP-5862 - След корабля Фолкнера</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/regarding-scp-5862">SCP-5862 - След корабля Фолкнера » Об SCP-5862</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-2834">SCP-2834 Кровь МЕХАН</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>French -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/scp-5501">SCP-5501</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Traditional Chinese -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-zh-tr.wikidot.com/nancy-shoe">LaRue 海報 - 南希的鞋子</a> - Nancy's Shoe</li> <li><a href="http://scp-zh-tr.wikidot.com/larue-post-bang">LaRue 海報 - 砰!</a> - Bang!</li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">I &lt;3 the Circus</span></span></h4> <p>This tale series is the introduction of a few new Circus characters. While it isn't explicit throughout the story (so far), the Protagonist eventually attains the name Cahaya. The relationship between Cahaya and Fraust is really the first thing I've added to the site, and I'm quite glad that the first thing I put in is a love story. It starts with the I &lt;3 the Circus, and then ends with <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4459">SCP-4459: The Ringmaster's Crown</a>. Time is funky, because in my headcanon, the Kaleidoscope allows for opening Ways into the past.</p> <p>Some of the feedback I've gotten has been about how forced the gender stuff appears. Cahaya is meant to be whatever gender you assign to them. I wanted it to be very fluid on that. Also, Fraust is a Clown, and can change their gender at will. Sooo, yeah. Gender fluidity is deeply personal to me, and I wanted to showcase that in my stories about these people.</p> <p>I'd like to dedicate all of these stories to my beloved boyfriend. He's an acrobat/contortionist/aerialist in the real-world circus, and my love for him is intermixed with my love of Herman Fuller's Circus. Thank you for being such a light in my life, and for your unfailing love and support. You give me the strength to continue, to be better, to be worthy. &lt;3</p> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">SCP-5501: Empty Portraits</span></span></h4> <p>This represents a significant amount of research into the American Civil War as well as the impact of that conflict upon the mental health of the people that participated. As one of the bloodiest periods of my nation's history, the impact of that war has etched itself deeply upon the collective psyche of the people that survived it and the descendants.</p> <p>I am a first generation American. Both sides of my parental lineage stretch far back through centuries of conflict and death, so while I cannot say that the echoes of the American Civil War still ring in my blood, I see the horrors of my own cultural legacy mirrored in it.</p> <p>While I am excited to write fiction about these events, I think it is tremendously important to keep in mind that these events happened. There is no horror that I can craft in the comfort of my office chair that will ever match the horror experienced by the people that fought and died in that war, or any war. Out of respect, I have kept as close to the source material as possible.</p> <p>All of the officers mentioned here are real people. The battles and dates of the battles mentioned here are real. The only one that wasn't is &quot;Massacre at Seven Pines&quot;, that is entirely of my creation. The horror of The Battle of The Crater is real, and the racism that added to that needless slaughter was also real.</p> <p>Let us not forget that this war was fought, and a great many people died, for the &quot;right&quot; of the Southern States to own slaves. This horrific stain on my Nation's history must never be forgotten lest we become complacent, and thus complicit, in the practice of trafficking and sale of human beings all around the globe.</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p>Here are some Authors I think you should check out:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/hammermaidens-author-page">HammerMaiden</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/themightymcb-s-author-page">TheMightyMcB</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/doctor-s-s-personnel-file">SoullessSingularity</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/dr-john-peppersghost-pepper-s-personnel-file">PeppersGhost</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/manymeats">ManyMeats</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.wikidot.com/drakimoto-s-author-page">DrAkimoto</a></li> </ul> <hr /> <p>My favorites:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-4140">SCP-4140: Sarkic Containment Procedures</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-2000">SCP-2000: Deus Ex Machina</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-4203">SCP-4203: Sometimes a Damselfly Just Wants Some Dick</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-2264">SCP-2264: In the Court of Alagadda</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1921">SCP-1921: Black Cotton Candy</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1921">SCP-4840: The Demon Lancelot and the Flying City of Audapaupadopolis</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5805">SCP-5805: You Can't Go Back</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/the-foundation-eats-babies">Tales of the Ethics Committee: The Foundation Eats Babies</a></li> </ul> <hr /></div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-3" style="display:none"> <h3><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">If I am Gone</span></span></h3> <p>In the event that I have disappeared off of the wiki and IRC for a period longer than 6 months without any notice or updates, I entrust the curation of all my solo <em>La Rue Macabre</em> content to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187161&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606963615" alt="plaidypus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187161)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" >plaidypus</a></span>, all my other solo stuff to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5255688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606963615" alt="DrAkimoto" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5255688)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" >DrAkimoto</a></span>, and my collaborative articles with their respective co-authors.</p> <p>These curators are expressly allowed to make substantive modifications to my work, provided it doesn't change the overall theme of the piece. (An Alagaddan skip will remain Alaggadan, etc.)</p> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">If Anybody Needs Me</span></span></h4> <p>In the event that somebody on the wiki needs me and I am not responding to Wikidot PMs or IRC, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606963615" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span> has my personal cell number and can communicate with me offline.</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-4" style="display:none"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:135%;"><strong>All my artwork can be found at <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-graveyard">The Graveyard</a></strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <h3><span>From <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6001754&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606963615" alt="barredowl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6001754)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" >barredowl</a></span>:</span></h3> <h3><span>Because I am a practicing Sar-kick.</span></h3> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border: 1px solid #000;"> <div style="height: 100%;"> <div class="image-container aligncenter"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/malycegraves-author/frombarredowl.png" title="Because I am a practicing Sar-kick." alt="Because I am a practicing Sar-kick." width="400px" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <h3><span>SCP-5501</span></h3> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border: 1px solid #000;"> <div style="height: 100%;"> <div class="image-container aligncenter"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl-s-kick-ass-art-page/5501.png" title="SCP-5501" alt="SCP-5501" width="400px" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <h3><span>From <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5950867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606963615" alt="KaraKatt" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5950867)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" >KaraKatt</a></span>:</span></h3> <h3><span>I have acquired a crow-lich familiar</span></h3> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border: 1px solid #000;"> <div style="height: 100%;"> <div class="image-container aligncenter"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/malycegraves-author/malyceandkara.png" title="I have acquired a crow-lich familiar" alt="I